# Optional: enables the "Connect Google Drive" import flow.
# Create an OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application) in Google Cloud Console,
# add your dev/prod origins under "Authorized JavaScript origins", and
# enable the Google Drive API for the project. This ID is public (it's sent
# to the browser) — no client secret is needed since SimpleSet uses Google
# Identity Services' client-side token flow.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Optional: enables AI-assisted PDF import (the paid tier) and account
# creation/sign-in. From your Supabase project's Settings -> API. The anon
# key is public (safe to ship to the browser) — it only grants what Row
# Level Security and the "parse" Edge Function allow. Without these, PDF
# import falls back to basic local text parsing and /auth shows a
# "not configured" message.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
